{"ok": true, "messages": [{"ts": "1759249488.495439", "type": "message", "text": "i think we should squeeze in the fix for that issue if it's an easy fix. annoying and players can see that for 10 times in a day if they make it that far.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1759249488.495439"}, {"ts": "1758905363.341129", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0032_SLACK_ID> The iOS memory seems like a guess. Will LiveOps to addressables do the trick you think? Do we have to go after the objects and monsters?

I should note that we currently don't have addressables in ZM. We will need to set up the addressable manager stuff from DD. So There is some more lifting than just making things into an addressable.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758903616.346579", "type": "message", "text": "After I skipped the zombie lane tutorial, ı got the exception and skipping couldn’t claim the ice cream. <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID>   ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758903616.346579"}, {"ts": "1758827960.705049", "type": "message", "text": "and both colliders are equal", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827946.430599", "type": "message", "text": "I was able to see this one in my first play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827933.392849", "type": "message", "text": "which may cause performance issues as the colliders are quite complex", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827921.413599", "type": "message", "text": "looks like we can have objects that have more than 1 click collider", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827895.596809", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823160.030389", "type": "message", "text": "It could very well be an OS bug that we can't fix.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823142.221059", "type": "message", "text": "I think on Samsung devices, when you trigger that prompt, or about to, it disables the audio, because the permission dialog is an OS window, and it's an equivalent of homing out. So the app thinks it's in the background, at least from an audio standpoint", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823108.379949", "type": "message", "text": "OK Fortress Merge also has the weird sound bug. So I was playing, and suddenly my audio disappears... I don't know why, nothing happened on screen. Then I force quit and restart my app, the moment I restart, I get the Push notification permission prompt.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758767858.307829", "type": "message", "text": "Yeah go for it. Once it’s merged we can trigger a testflight build and then can submit to Apple. It will take a few days to go live ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765800.031519", "type": "message", "text": "do you think we can update the build version that the players are testing so we can gather new data?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765779.197199", "type": "message", "text": "and also added a skip tutorial button that appears after 10 seconds in the same tutorial step", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765741.130789", "type": "message", "text": "meaning the tutorial isnt showing anymore and the player is free to play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765726.644559", "type": "message", "text": "Not in the logs... I added a new analytics event that is invoked when the tutorial object is destroyed", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758763902.253029", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Any updates on the bugs? See anything strange?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758751463.920129", "type": "message", "text": "it’s a known thing that some event packs get dropped for some users occasioanlly, it happens to every game every user. It’s supposed to be a small percent but it happens - just a reminder on this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758751463.920129"}, {"ts": "1758746963.720009", "type": "message", "text": "And it's evident There was a restart because of the login and splash screen after level 2, but the left_level 2 event never fired off, so it would suggest that it's a pretty severe crash that the app can't even send off anything", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758746963.720009"}, {"ts": "1758746923.853549", "type": "message", "text": "This tells me There was a gap in their log, like Leonard's friend", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758746915.653289", "type": "message", "text": "I think something at the start of a level is crashing people, this user, started level 3, didn't finish level 3, but they have a begin level 2 event, but no left level 2 event, despite being able to start level 3:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744890.526289", "type": "message", "text": "Invisible button", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744887.062759", "type": "message", "text": "Time based, I dont know", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744881.531029", "type": "message", "text": "And something that allows them to skip tutorial", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741900.550579", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> can you add track item match too?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019", "subtype": "thread_broadcast"}, {"ts": "1758741639.564949", "type": "message", "text": "just to discard the possibility", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741621.195989", "type": "message", "text": "we could even disable tutorials completely", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741498.293709", "type": "message", "text": "Maybe even 50% of the users are hit by this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741473.290079", "type": "message", "text": "But the gist is that I would say 25% of the players are hit by this issue between level 3, 4, and 5. Once you make it through you're probably gonna be OK. So it's like a filter for buggy users", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741426.226829", "type": "message", "text": "Im adding more events to track correctness of each step that can act as blocker", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741424.791859", "type": "message", "text": "It could be some sort of initialization of something", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.330639", "type": "message", "text": "I dont even think it is the FTUE anymore, I might be wrong though", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.079659", "type": "message", "text": "But if it says "stop game" or "enemy start", I am unclear as to what happened next", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741399.304189", "type": "message", "text": "I would assume if they quit at "Waiting for highlight to fade", it's likely they didn't get to match a single item", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741334.346719", "type": "message", "text": "Because all these "crashes" it's a bit unclear the FTUE happened, did they just get stuck? Or were they at least able to match some items before restarting", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741305.545019", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Is There a good way to just record actual item click on or a set of item was removed from the board as an event? And we just plug it into level 1-5", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019"}, {"ts": "1758738754.255909", "type": "message", "text": "Leonard also had a friend, that had his game froze for good, and had to restart his app. This was during his first attempt at endless mode level. The log registered NOTHING. Meaning we didn't see him start/stop endless level, even though every user is forced to play it at least once.  Once Leonard's friend restarted, his log just continued to the next level, as if he skipped several steps, a giant gap in his log, like he got his drink spiked.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758738690.388049", "type": "message", "text": "So a lot of the problems we are seeing, is we see user engagement events happening mid level, or numerous times, repeatedly, at odd intervals. We were able to confirm that user_engagement event is working as it should. Our play test cloud video literally had a lady that took a face time call at level 7, and sure enough that backgrounding of the app created a user engagement event right on the dot.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758738635.046079", "type": "message", "text": "Google truncates the user session with a "user_engagement" which records the duration of that session. The truncate happens when the app is put into the background for 1 second or more", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737369.238919", "type": "message", "text": "user engagement means the game is stopped with various reasons, it can be a phone call, checking notifications, putting app to the background pr killing the app etc. then it sums up seconds between two user engagement event", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737276.062599", "type": "message", "text": "do we know if the users with problems also stop in the user_engagement step?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737253.190019", "type": "message", "text": "well", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736831.675709", "type": "message", "text": "healthy user also looks like that.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736773.947609", "type": "message", "text": "could you check if level 3 is the same as this in a normal user?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736639.991969", "type": "message", "text": "I need to see how it looks in a healthy user", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736629.392479", "type": "message", "text": "because he was able to start lvl 4 without problem", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736612.708059", "type": "message", "text": "I might be wrong in my assumption", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736603.541169", "type": "message", "text": "so why do you think they dont have an issue in Level 3?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736579.722089", "type": "message", "text": "but none of them are finished in later steps", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736567.088209", "type": "message", "text": "the input is blocked and the highlight opens", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736552.780329", "type": "message", "text": "on level 3 it doesnt happen", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736495.468569", "type": "message", "text": "and then CloseHighlight closing it", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736488.954989", "type": "message", "text": "you can also see WaitHightlightFadeOut opening the highlight window", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736459.437829", "type": "message", "text": "you can see that BlockInput is called 2 times, one to block and another one to unblock", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736438.382539", "type": "message", "text": "this is level 2", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736437.674779", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736434.036549", "type": "message", "text": "look", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736432.723139", "type": "message", "text": "I think they do", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736377.317639", "type": "message", "text": "we can either be using some #if UNITY_ANDROID and executing something important only for android
or There is some platform difference in something that the tutorial does", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736374.596719", "type": "message", "text": "I think player don't have any issue in level 3", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736362.701629", "type": "message", "text": "is it tho?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736320.935089", "type": "message", "text": "hard to say what would fix it since it is hard to repro", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736300.571769", "type": "message", "text": "I'll look for a potential fix now :[USERNAME_3620]:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736286.703599", "type": "message", "text": "good thing we figured out the potential issue", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736155.448849", "type": "message", "text": "on level 3 it never closes for some reason", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736144.833699", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736109.564909", "type": "message", "text": "when highlight works correctly, it closes eventually", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736099.390729", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736066.571839", "type": "message", "text": "have a look at this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736060.875149", "type": "message", "text": "the problem seems to be the highlight", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758736053.499159", "type": "message", "text": "yeah", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758735704.757069", "type": "message", "text": "is this exportable to a sheet or something?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758735704.757069"}, {"ts": "1758735695.609099", "type": "message", "text": "sure thing", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758735677.043699", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Can you look at this log and let me know if you can think of anything? You see how the player attempted level 4 several times, and simply can't even play it. First it's probably some FTUE related glitch, and restarting the app several times didn't seem to work:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758735677.043699"}, {"ts": "1758734347.505159", "type": "message", "text": "<https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/dashboard/595-zombie-match-dashboard?ab_default=&amp;ab_mf=&amp;app_version=0.3.36&amp;app_version=0.3.38&amp;lawson40=&amp;country=&amp;country_tier_=Tier+1&amp;d0_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;date=&amp;developer_or_customer=&amp;level_%28only_impacts_left_level_tables%29=&amp;platform_%28ios%252C_and%29=IOS&amp;total_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;user_source=Unity+Ads|https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/dashboard/595-zombie-match-dashboard?ab_default=&amp;ab_mf[…]OS&amp;total_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;user_source=Unity+Ads>", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758734341.737279", "type": "message", "text": "<https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/dashboard/595-zombie-match-dashboard?ab_default=&amp;ab_mf=&amp;app_version=0.3.127&amp;lawson40=&amp;country=&amp;country_tier_=Tier+1&amp;d0_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;date=&amp;developer_or_customer=&amp;level_%28only_impacts_left_level_tables%29=&amp;platform_%28ios%252C_and%29=&amp;total_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;user_source=Unity+Ads|https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/dashboard/595-zombie-match-dashboard?ab_default=&amp;ab_mf[…]9=&amp;total_%2523_of_levels_played=&amp;user_source=Unity+Ads>", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758642623.835409", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID> let's share our crash notes here:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758642623.835409"}, {"ts": "1758637301.299449", "type": "message", "text": "And adjust bosses killed because we're using the trick to make all zombies bosses", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0005_SLACK_ID"}], "has_more": false, "response_metadata": {"next_cursor": ""}}

{"ok": true, "messages": [{"ts": "1758848169.753889", "type": "message", "text": "The code looks like it plays both at the same time. Ok. If [USERNAME_37176] says it's good then it's good.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758840125.902539", "type": "message", "text": "It basically queue all tutorials found at that lvl and plays it 1 by 1", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758840097.470729", "type": "message", "text": "[PERSON_NAME_0050] tested and didn't find any problem", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758840074.109269", "type": "message", "text": "I made a change for that because There're multiple tutorials that was at lvl 16... Which introduced the zombie lane and the card tutorial, I put them in queue and to be played once everything finished in queue manager, before it was only running the 1st tutorial it encountered", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838449.812699", "type": "message", "text": "We can leave it for now but just think about how we might fix it.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838413.466729", "type": "message", "text": "If we were to start multiple tutorials it would be def be a problem.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838333.037069", "type": "message", "text": "Ok.  The AI made a comment about the tutorial queuing multiple at once.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758836409.995169", "type": "message", "text": "Done, I pushed that change :[USERNAME_1653]:", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835929.106509", "type": "message", "text": "let me apply that change", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835920.233189", "type": "message", "text": "looks very promising :[USERNAME_1653]: .. I'll try it for next time", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835883.164369", "type": "message", "text": "Yeah I think I get it.. just a key for any VFX triggered, instead of resetting lvl complete value. :thinking_face:", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0006_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835593.463079", "type": "message", "text": "I think something like this might be cleaner:
```private void PlayLevelCompleteVFX()
{
    if (LevelManager.Instance.HasCompletedPreviousLevel())
    {
        // Check if VFX has already been shown for this level
        int currentLevel = PlayerPrefs.GetInt("Level", 0);
        string vfxKey = $"LevelCompleteVFX_Shown_{currentLevel}";

        if (!PlayerPrefs.GetInt(vfxKey, 0).Equals(1))
        {
            BlockInput();
            Debug.Log("[RewardVFXManager] Detected level completed. Playing coin VFX...");

            var req = new RewardVFXRequest
            {
                Type = ERewardType.Coins,
                Amount = CoinsManager.CoinsPerWin,
                Anchor = transform,
                WorldPosition = transform.position,
                WorldRotation = Quaternion.identity,
                HasWorldPose = true
            };

            PlayBatch(new List&lt;RewardVFXRequest&gt; { req });

            // Mark VFX as shown for this level
            PlayerPrefs.SetInt(vfxKey, 1);
            PlayerPrefs.Save();
        }
    }
}```", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835569.151229", "type": "message", "text": "Back to the PR review. It seems very weird that a [USERNAME_37174] would be resetting what the LastLevelCompleted is.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835511.171779", "type": "message", "text": "I was copying and pasting from chatgpt before but this is 10x better.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835497.424999", "type": "message", "text": "for example you put it in ‘agent’ mode and just say:

Build me a notification manager with these features and hook it up with level complete blah blah blah.

